<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mari</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mari was an ancient city on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, a major trading centre in the early second millennium BCE. Its palace archives are a key source for the diplomacy of the age, including relations between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> and other powers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> of Babylon sacked Mari in 1761 BCE and destroyed its famous palace.</p></div>
